      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Given that $P(C|A)=0.6,$ $P(A)=0.4,$ and $P(C)=0.3,$ compute $P(A|C).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A|C) & =\\frac{P(C|A)P(A)}{P(C)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.6)(0.4)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.24}{0.3} \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
